audit.payload:
$domains = @(Get-AcceptedDomain)
$results = foreach ($d in $domains) { $record = (Resolve-DnsName -Name "_dmarc.$($d.DomainName)" -Type TXT).Strings; [pscustomobject]@{ Domain = $d.DomainName; Record = $record; Compliant = ($record -match 'p=(quarantine|reject)') -and ($record -match 'rua=') } }
[pscustomobject]@{ Domains = @($results); NonCompliant = @($results | Where-Object { -not $_.Compliant } | ForEach-Object { $_.Domain }) } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 6 -Compress

controls.remediationProcedure:
Set-HostedContentFilterPolicy -Identity <Policy name> -AllowedSenderDomains @{}
Or, run this to remove allowed domains from all inbound anti-spam policies:
$AllowedDomains = Get-HostedContentFilterPolicy | Where-Object { $_.AllowedSenderDomains } 
$AllowedDomains | Set-HostedContentFilterPolicy -AllowedSenderDomains @{}
